{
  "id": "19d22654-aea9-4e6e-b441-b9c9f19b7c44",
  "title": "Unified Framework for Medical Image Segmentation with Uncertainty-Aware Techniques",
  "summary": "A post-hoc framework (SegWithU) that augments a frozen segmentation backbone with a lightweight uncertainty head, modeling uncertainty as perturbation energy in a compact probe space. It achieves state-of-the-art performance across multiple benchmark datasets, demonstrating robustness and efficiency in reliability-aware medical segmentation. The other report discusses the differentiable shift-variant FBP model for cone-beam CT, highlighting its efficiency and robustness under challenging acquisition settings.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "SegWithU combines human-in-the-loop annotation, cardiac CT augmentation, and self-supervised models to enhance cardiac CT segmentation and phenotyping.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SegWithU models uncertainty as perturbation energy in a compact probe space, achieving superior accuracy and scalability compared to existing tools.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The framework addresses domain shift challenges and provides a reproducible foundation for population-level phenotyping.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
